{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cecthj4ud3D4ZmQmtbyrq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 3 tests pass now — no test was deleted or skipped.\n\nThe failure was a real tokenizer bug, not a flaky test, so I fixed it instead of skipping it (masking it would have shipped broken behavior: any t-string containing a nested f-string in its `{...}` expression would mis-tokenize everything after the nested f-string as f-string tokens instead of t-string tokens). Root cause in `src/pytokens/__init__.py`: `FStringState.is_template` was a single flag that wasn't properly saved/restored across nested string levels.\n\nFix (two related issues in the same code path):\n1. `push_fstring_prefix_quote`/`pop_fstring_quote` now save/restore `is_template` alongside the prefix/quote stack, so it's per-nesting-level instead of global.\n2. In `fstring()`, the outer `is_template` was being overwritten *before* being pushed onto the stack (so the stack captured the wrong value) — reordered to push first, then set the new value.\n3. In the `at_fstring_end` handler, the closing token is now built *before* popping the stack, so the closing token itself still reflects the string that's actually closing, not the one it's returning to."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":542,"cache_read_input_tokens":58758,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":542},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"54e9d7c1-1345-5e2d-ba67-93201e1134e8","uuid":"f99f3078-4861-4d9c-bf83-2eee672228ab","timestamp":"2026-09-01T14:39:50.715Z","request_id":"req_011CecthiALXKJBfitgG75Sf"}
